Spoilers for Magicbane's powers and other stun effect weapons.  (Does 
Slash'em have a cattle prod?)

Causing a stun effect with Magicbane seemed to be more useful to me than 
other posters were indicating.  So I code dived for a while and it turns 
out that stunning makes monsters more likely to cast spells.

Since Magicbane is a very effective spell defense (especially when 
combined with the crowning resistances and reflection) this causes the 
hostile monster to waste time while standing next to you.  Which is 
always a good thing.

